#4471 was merged as one issue and marked known: the parser reads dates month first, and our
day-first tenants write day first. Reading the reports it merged against the tenant directory,
with the desk's own cause logic, shows the ticket covers more than the one issue it names.

## The split

<SplitTable ticket={4471} />

<Callout kind="warn">
The desk's table still says one cause. The hint cause has no ticket of its own, and the one-day
moves were footnoted, not filed.
</Callout>

## What each problem is

**parser** — the shared parser reads every date month first. A day-first tenant's dates come out
with the month and the day flipped. This is the bug the ticket names, and the fix is queued.

**hint** — through the booking-v3 form, the hint under the date field prints month first. The
tenant's people type what the hint tells them, and the form reads it the tenant's way. The flip
happens in the form, not in the parser: a different bug. A queued parser fix will not cover it.

**one-day move** — the booking lands one day off, not a month off. An invite that says Tuesday
shows as Monday, and one meeting showed Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto, and the company
held it twice. None of the five bodies describe a month and day flip.

